    "headline": "THE MIDDLE OF THE SEASON JUST GOT MEAN",
    "deck": "Two teams sit at 5-1, four more are 4-2, and Week 6 delivered everything from a 1.78-point escape to a 66.92-64.12 rock fight. The runway to the postseason is getting crowded.",
    "story": [
      "Redwood Murder and California Un-Named Team leave Week 6 with matching 5-1 records, but the pack is stacked directly behind them. Turbulent Ticklesh!ts, Sullco MethMouths, Simpson Sith and Eskimo Brothers are all 4-2. Nobody at the top has earned breathing room.",
      "THE Barton Spartans authored the week\u2019s biggest scoring jolt at 114.10, while Turbulent Ticklesh!ts landed only half a point behind at 113.60. Your Mom survived Space Cadets 109.74-107.96 in the closest game of the week, the kind of result that begins to feel enormous once the standings compress.",
      "And then there was California Un-Named Team versus Flint Tropics: 66.92-64.12. California escaped with the win and moved to 5-1 despite finishing next-to-last in Week 6 scoring. Flint dropped to 0-6 despite coming within 2.80 points of knocking off one of the league leaders. Fantasy football has a sick sense of humor.",
      "Underneath the records, Turbulent Ticklesh!ts and Sullco MethMouths continue to look dangerous. Through six completed weeks they own the two best all-play marks at 47-19 and 46-20, respectively. Off Boys sits only 3-3 head-to-head but carries a 44-22 all-play record, making them the kind of .500 team nobody should mistake for harmless."
